// The starship from the original series, built part by part from the plans and the studio model.
//
//     import 'enterprise' { Enterprise }
//
//     object Enterprise(289)
//
// | `Enterprise` | The whole ship: saucer, dorsal, secondary hull, pylons and nacelles, in detail. |
// | `EnterpriseSaucer`, `EnterpriseSecondaryHull` | Her two halves, in the plans' own frame. |
// | `EnterpriseNacelle`, `EnterpriseImpulseEngines` | Two of the parts they are built from. |
//
// **The first number is a length**, in **meters**, and she **faces `+X`** with her origin in her own
// middle -- the conventions of the [spacecraft](#spacecraft), for the same reason: she rests on nothing,
// so an origin in the middle is what lets `rotate` turn her about herself.  289 is the published figure,
// and `long` scales her whole.  `variant` is taken for the same uniformity and does nothing; there was
// one of her.
//
// -- Where the shape comes from -----------------------------------------------------------------------
//
// Franz Joseph's Booklet of General Plans: the saucer's profile and cutaway, the secondary hull's
// profile, top, bottom and rear views and the cutaway of its nose, the dorsal's section, and the
// nacelle's profile, top and bottom.  Every part was traced from scans of those sheets, which measure
// 580.4 pixels to one of the model's units -- the reason a few comments below give a fit in pixels.
//
// **Where the plans and the studio model disagree, the studio model wins.**  The control reactor's
// recess and the reactor in it, the intercoolers' height, the inset webs under them and the vents are
// taken from photographs of the original model, not from the plans.
//
// -- Her own frame ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//
// The parts are written in the plans' units with **+X aft**, the saucer's axis on Y and its rim at
// y = 0, so the saucer is 12.625 across and the whole ship 29.61 long from the saucer's rim to the
// nacelles' end caps.  `Enterprise` turns her about to face +X, moves her middle to the origin and scales
// her to meters, so a scene never sees this frame; it is here for a scene that wants one part alone.
//
// -- Her colors ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//
// **The hull plating has no material of its own**, so it takes what the scene gives the object: a
// material on `object Enterprise(...)` repaints the plating and leaves alone every part that names its
// color -- the deflector's orange, the copper of the inner cups and the antenna, the bronze of the
// Bussard domes, and the matte gray of the vanes, the reactor's recess, the vents, the grooves and the
// nacelles' hoods.  Unpainted, she is the default white.
//
// **A glow is a material at `ambient 1`** -- the impulse ports and the homing beacon -- and its color is
// the one it shows under one white light.  Every light adds its own ambient, in proportion to its own
// color: a second light at full strength makes a glow twice as bright, and a dim fill adds a little.

// -- Her parts, in the plans' frame -------------------------------------------------------------------

EnterpriseImpulseEngines = union {
    difference {
        union {
            intersection {
                tapered extrusion {
                    taper 0.777778
                    path {
                        // drawn 1.125 times the old base, about this half's own taper axis, so that the taper
                        // (0.875/1.125 over the height of 1) passes through exactly the old base at y = 0 and
                        // the old top at y = 0.5; below y = 0 it carries on at the same lean to meet the rim
                        move to 0.694443, 0
                        line to 2.693748, 0
                        curve 2.800538, 0, 2.887108, -0.08657 to 2.887108, -0.193359
                        curve 2.887108, -0.300149, 2.800538, -0.386719 to 2.693748, -0.386719
                        line to 0.694443, -0.386719
                        close
                    }
                    min Y -0.5
                    max Y 0.5
                    translate [-0.894443, 0, 0]
                }
                cube {
                    // keeps x >= 0 only: the half is clipped where it meets its twin
                    scale [2, 1, 1]
                    translate [2, 0.25, -0.17]
                }
            }
            intersection {
                tapered extrusion {
                    taper 0.777778
                    path {
                        // drawn 1.125 times the old base, about this half's own taper axis, so that the taper
                        // (0.875/1.125 over the height of 1) passes through exactly the old base at y = 0 and
                        // the old top at y = 0.5; below y = 0 it carries on at the same lean to meet the rim
                        move to -0.694443, 0
                        line to -2.693748, 0
                        curve -2.800538, 0, -2.887108, -0.08657 to -2.887108, -0.193359
                        curve -2.887108, -0.300149, -2.800538, -0.386719 to -2.693748, -0.386719
                        line to -0.694443, -0.386719
                        close
                    }
                    min Y -0.5
                    max Y 0.5
                    translate [0.894443, 0, 0]
                }
                cube {
                    // keeps x <= 0 only: the half is clipped where it meets its twin
                    scale [2, 1, 1]
                    translate [-2, 0.25, -0.17]
                }
            }
        }

        // The exhaust ports: two plain rectangles cut into the aft face (the extrusion's small end, at
        // y = 0.5), their outer edges 0.745543 out from the middle and their inner edges 0.14 out, so
        // each is 0.605543 wide (22.4% of the face's 2.702171) with 0.28 between them;
        // inset 0.05 from the face's top and bottom edges, and 0.07 deep.  Each cutter pokes 0.02 out
        // past the face so the two never share a surface.  The cutters take the hull's material, so
        // the walls of each recess shade like the rest of the block and the depth can be seen.
        cube {
            scale [0.302771, 0.045, 0.100391]
            translate [0.442771, 0.475, -0.150391]
        }
        cube {
            scale [0.302771, 0.045, 0.100391]
            translate [-0.442771, 0.475, -0.150391]
        }
    }

    // The glow at the back of each port: a thin plate a little larger than the opening, so its edges are
    // buried in the recess walls, with its face 0.004 proud of the recess floor.  A flat, self-lit
    // yellow-orange, its own color under one white light (see the header on glows and lights).
    cube {
        scale [0.307771, 0.012, 0.105391]
        translate [0.442771, 0.422, -0.150391]
        material {
            pigment [1, 0.5, 0.05]          // as it shows under one white light
            ambient 1
            diffuse 0
            specular 0
        }
    }
    cube {
        scale [0.307771, 0.012, 0.105391]
        translate [-0.442771, 0.422, -0.150391]
        material {
            pigment [1, 0.5, 0.05]          // as it shows under one white light
            ambient 1
            diffuse 0
            specular 0
        }
    }
    rotate X -90
    rotate Y -90
}

EnterpriseSaucer = union {
    lathe {
        path {
            move to 0, 0.46875
            quad -2.3362542, 0.46875 to -4.625, 0
            line to -6.3125, 0
    
            // the rim face: straight, raked back, dr/dh = 0.5156
            line to -6.0444, -0.5200
    
            // the underside: it undercuts behind the rim, cresting at h = -0.465 near r = 4.3,
            // then falls away and levels off at mid deck 11 (h = -1.3930, reached at r = 1.20)
            quad -6.0084, -0.5899 to -5.9297, -0.5899
            line to -5.6000, -0.5899
            quad -5.4164, -0.5899 to -5.2500, -0.5580
            quad -4.7624, -0.4647 to -4.3000, -0.4647
            quad -3.6132, -0.4571 to -3.0000, -0.6392
            quad -2.5506, -0.7906 to -2.1000, -1.0048
            quad -1.7238, -1.1712 to -1.3500, -1.3381
            quad -1.2270, -1.3930 to -1.0924, -1.3930
    
            // flat along mid deck 11, then square down the leading wall of deck 11
            line to -0.9450, -1.3930
            line to -0.9450, -1.4635
    
            // a pronounced turn from that wall into the floor of deck 11
            quad -0.9450, -1.5335 to -0.8450, -1.5335
            line to -0.8150, -1.5335
    
            // the rib: a U as thick as it is deep, its right side turning horizontal where the
            // dome starts, and that horizontal running in to the axis
            line to -0.8150, -1.5710
            quad -0.7775, -1.6460 to -0.7400, -1.5710
            line to -0.7400, -1.5335
            line to  0.0000, -1.5335
            close
        }
    }
    egg {
        radii 1.56, 1.17
        scale X 0.5
        rotate Z -90
        translate [-0.2, 0.30775, 0]
    }
    lathe {
        path {
            // the bridge: a flat roof, a quarter-elliptical corner (two quads, one per 45 degrees)
            // and a straight front wall.  The corner leaves the roof where the cutaway has it, 0.215
            // in from the wall, and meets the wall a third of the way up from the egg at the bow;
            // the cutaway's own corner is a circle meeting the wall at 1.16, but the egg sits lower
            // than the drawn deck there, and a circle would leave too much wall showing.
            move to 0, 1.3750
            line to -0.7640, 1.3750
            quad -0.8531, 1.3750 to -0.9160, 1.2986
            quad -0.9790, 1.2221 to -0.9790, 1.1140

            // the wall runs on down into the egg: the egg's top falls as low as 0.935 under the
            // bridge's rim, so stopping at the drawing's deck (1.09) would leave a gap
            line to -0.9790, 0.8500
            line to  0.0000, 0.8500
            close
        }
    }
    lathe {
        // the upper sensor dome: a spherical cap on the bridge roof, in the proportion to the bridge
        // that the cutaway draws the two (base 0.644, rise 0.156).  Its foot sinks a little into
        // the roof so the two never share a surface.
        path {
            move to 0, 1.5314
            quad -0.1680, 1.5314 to -0.3312, 1.4918
            quad -0.4945, 1.4521 to -0.6437, 1.3750
            line to -0.6437, 1.3600
            line to  0.0000, 1.3600
            close
        }
        material {
            pigment CosmicLatte
        }
    }
    lathe {
        // the lower sensor dome: a spherical cap hanging inside the rib, starting right where the
        // rib's inner side turns horizontal (r = 0.740), and as deep for its width as the cutaway
        // draws it (0.162).  Its top rises a little into the hull so the two never share a surface.
        path {
            move to 0, -1.5200
            line to -0.7400, -1.5200
            line to -0.7400, -1.5335
            quad -0.5659, -1.6135 to -0.3787, -1.6544
            quad -0.1916, -1.6953 to 0, -1.6953
            close
        }
        material {
            pigment CosmicLatte
        }
    }
    cylinder {
        // the bridge's elevator housing: at the back of the bridge, its centre 98% of the way out
        // to the bridge's rim as the cutaway draws it, so it straddles the bridge's aft wall; its
        // top stands just proud of the roof, and its foot is buried in the egg (whose top is 1.025
        // at the lowest under it)
        min Y 0.85
        max Y 1.385
        scale [0.183, 1, 0.183]
        translate [0.960, 0, 0]
    }
    // The rib that runs aft from the egg to the impulse housing, built from the blueprints the way a
    // shape is recovered from its views: the plan, the profile and the rear view each pushed out into a
    // prism, and the rib is what all three have in common.  Heights are the blueprints' own, above the
    // housing's top, less the 0.02 the housing sits below the saucer's.  The rear view's pill stands
    // taller than the profile's crest (0.232 against 0.176); its heights are scaled by 0.784 to meet the
    // profile, and its widths kept.
    intersection {
        extrusion {
            // the plan: a rounded front, a straight taper, and a flare into two rounded ears at the
            // housing's aft face (just inside it, so the two never share a surface)
            path {
                move to 3.357, 0
                curve 3.357, 0.0913, 3.3966, 0.332 to 3.72, 0.3163
                line to 6.18, 0.1971
                curve 6.3121, 0.1907, 6.5003, 0.172 to 6.7225, 0.3288
                curve 6.7394, 0.3408, 6.7616, 0.3423 to 6.78, 0.3328
                curve 6.7984, 0.3232, 6.81, 0.3042 to 6.81, 0.2835
                line to 6.81, -0.2835
                curve 6.81, -0.3042, 6.7984, -0.3232 to 6.78, -0.3328
                curve 6.7616, -0.3423, 6.7394, -0.3408 to 6.7225, -0.3288
                curve 6.5003, -0.172, 6.3121, -0.1907 to 6.18, -0.1971
                line to 3.72, -0.3163
                curve 3.3966, -0.332, 3.357, -0.0913 to 3.357, 0
                close
            }
            min Y -0.05
            max Y 0.5
        }
        extrusion {
            // the profile: nearly level, then chamfered down to the aft face's top edge
            path {
                move to 3.2, -0.05
                line to 3.2, 0.1653
                line to 6.613, 0.1501
                line to 6.81, -0.02
                line to 6.81, -0.05
                close
            }
            min Y -1
            max Y 1
            rotate X -90
        }
        extrusion {
            // the rear view: the pill of the crest, the lobes either side, resting on the housing
            path {
                move to 0, 0.1619
                curve 0.032, 0.1619, 0.058, 0.1415 to 0.058, 0.1164
                line to 0.058, 0.1043
                curve 0.1835, 0.1046, 0.2558, 0.0941 to 0.2623, 0.0568
                line to 0.2623, 0.0455
                line to 0.297, 0.0455
                curve 0.3202, 0.0455, 0.339, 0.0309 to 0.339, 0.0128
                curve 0.339, -0.0053, 0.3202, -0.02 to 0.297, -0.02
                line to 0.297, -0.05
                line to -0.297, -0.05
                line to -0.297, -0.02
                curve -0.3202, -0.02, -0.339, -0.0053 to -0.339, 0.0128
                curve -0.339, 0.0309, -0.3202, 0.0455 to -0.297, 0.0455
                line to -0.2623, 0.0455
                line to -0.2623, 0.0568
                curve -0.2558, 0.0941, -0.1835, 0.1046 to -0.058, 0.1043
                line to -0.058, 0.1164
                curve -0.058, 0.1415, -0.032, 0.1619 to 0, 0.1619
                close
            }
            min Y -6.95
            max Y -3.2
            rotate X -90
            rotate Y 90
        }
    }
    object EnterpriseImpulseEngines {
        translate [6.3125, -0.02, 0] 
    }
}

// A warp nacelle, from FJ's nacelle profile, top and bottom (each sheet scanned in two halves and joined),
// in its own frame: the axis along X, the pylon's chord centered on the origin, up along Y and the inboard
// side toward -Z.  The drawings are at the hull's scale (the pylon root measures 1.000-1.010 against the
// pylon's 1.0045).  The two nacelles are this one placed, and this one mirrored.
EnterpriseNacelle = union {
    sphere {
        // the Bussard dome: half an ellipsoid, 0.81 along and 0.84 across (the drawings' ellipse exactly), in
        // an orange-red bronze.  Its aft half lies wholly inside the collar and the body.
        scale [0.8119, 0.8382, 0.8382]
        translate [-3.3330, 0, 0]
        material {
            pigment [0.6121, 0.0815, 0.0094]   // an orange-red bronze, (0.8, 0.32, 0.12) as it shows with gamma on
            diffuse 0.7
            specular 0.7
            shininess 35
            metallic 1
            brilliance 3
            reflective 0.15
        }
    }
    difference {
        lathe {
            // the body, from just inside the Bussard dome's rim back to the hood: a short chamfer out to the
            // collar, a recess under the vane ring, and a straight taper to the hood.  It starts a little
            // inside the dome, so the two never share a surface.
            path {
                move to 0, -3.3511
                line to 0.8339, -3.3511
                line to 0.8391, -3.3132
                line to 0.9063, -3.1943
                line to 0.9063, -2.8015
                line to 0.8615, -2.8015
                line to 0.8615, -2.5465
                line to 0.9034, -2.5465
                line to 0.6818, 10.6823
                line to 0, 10.6823
                close
            }
            rotate Z -90
        }
        intersection {
            // the recess the control reactor sits in, along the inboard side at mid-height, as the studio
            // model has it: 0.5341 tall, from the pylon's fore-and-aft centerline back to just ahead of the inboard vent.
            // Its walls slope in from the surface for 0.0793 at top and bottom, and between them the floor is
            // flat and vertical, 0.0948 below the surface; the floor leans in 0.960 degrees with the body's
            // taper, so the depth holds all the way aft.  It takes the vane rings' matte gray.
            extrusion {
                // its side outline: a long rectangle with rounded corners
                path {
                    move to 0.1034, -0.2671
                    line to 8.8560, -0.2671
                    curve 8.9131, -0.2671, 8.9593, -0.2208 to 8.9593, -0.1637
                    line to 8.9593, 0.1637
                    curve 8.9593, 0.2208, 8.9131, 0.2671 to 8.8560, 0.2671
                    line to 0.1034, 0.2671
                    curve 0.0463, 0.2671, 0.0000, 0.2208 to 0.0000, 0.1637
                    line to 0.0000, -0.1637
                    curve 0.0000, -0.2208, 0.0463, -0.2671 to 0.1034, -0.2671
                    close
                }
                min Y 0
                max Y 1.2
                rotate X -90
            }
            extrusion {
                // its section: the flat floor and the two sloped walls, carried along the nacelle's axis
                path {
                    move to -0.1878, -0.7659
                    line to 0.1878, -0.7659
                    line to 0.8550, -1.2061
                    line to -0.8550, -1.2061
                    close
                }
                min Y -1.5
                max Y 11
                rotate Z -90
                rotate Y -0.9596
            }
            material {
                pigment [0.1332, 0.1332, 0.1332]   // the vane rings' matte gray, 0.40 as it shows with gamma on
                specular 0
            }
        }
        // the two grooves round the end band, just aft of the vents, where FJ's profile draws its two lines:
        // each a torus centered on the body's surface, so the groove is 0.0241 wide and 0.0121 deep, and
        // cut in the vane rings' gray
        torus {
            // the fore groove
            radii 0.6853, 0.0121
            rotate Z 90
            translate [10.4686, 0, 0]
            material {
                pigment [0.1332, 0.1332, 0.1332]   // the vane rings' matte gray, 0.40 as it shows with gamma on
                specular 0
            }
        }
        torus {
            // the aft groove, clear of the hood's front
            radii 0.6820, 0.0121
            rotate Z 90
            translate [10.6685, 0, 0]
            material {
                pigment [0.1332, 0.1332, 0.1332]   // the vane rings' matte gray, 0.40 as it shows with gamma on
                specular 0
            }
        }
    }
    lathe {
        // the vane ring just aft of the Bussard dome: five ribs with shallow grooves between them, in a matte
        // gray.  Its front sits a little inside the collar and its back a little inside the body, over a
        // recess in the body, so it never shares a surface with either.
        path {
            move to 0, -2.8084
            line to 0.8890, -2.8084
            line to 0.8890, -2.7826
            line to 0.8787, -2.7826
            line to 0.8787, -2.7429
            line to 0.8890, -2.7429
            line to 0.8890, -2.7292
            line to 0.8787, -2.7292
            line to 0.8787, -2.6826
            line to 0.8890, -2.6826
            line to 0.8890, -2.6620
            line to 0.8787, -2.6620
            line to 0.8787, -2.6189
            line to 0.8890, -2.6189
            line to 0.8890, -2.5999
            line to 0.8787, -2.5999
            line to 0.8787, -2.5586
            line to 0.8890, -2.5586
            line to 0.8890, -2.5396
            line to 0, -2.5396
            close
        }
        rotate Z -90
        material {
            pigment [0.1332, 0.1332, 0.1332]   // a matte gray, 0.40 as it shows with gamma on
            specular 0
        }
    }
    difference {
        // the hood: the body's taper carried on aft, ribbed fore and aft and in the vane rings' gray, rounded
        // off in plan (a quarter ellipse 0.5699 long), with its lower aft part scooped away along the curve the
        // profile draws, from the bottom of the end band up to the hood's tip
        intersection {
            tapered extrusion {
                // the hood's skin: the body's taper carried on, fluted with 60 ribs running fore and aft, their
                // crests on the old surface and the grooves between them 0.0121 deep
                taper 0.97419
                path {
                    move to 0.6697, 0.0105
                    quad 0.6934, 0.0363 to 0.6671, 0.0595
                    line to 0.6649, 0.0805
                    quad 0.6858, 0.1086 to 0.6572, 0.1289
                    line to 0.6528, 0.1495
                    quad 0.6707, 0.1797 to 0.6401, 0.1969
                    line to 0.6336, 0.2169
                    quad 0.6482, 0.2488 to 0.6160, 0.2628
                    line to 0.6075, 0.2820
                    quad 0.6186, 0.3152 to 0.5852, 0.3257
                    line to 0.5747, 0.3439
                    quad 0.5823, 0.3781 to 0.5479, 0.3851
                    line to 0.5356, 0.4021
                    quad 0.5396, 0.4369 to 0.5047, 0.4403
                    line to 0.4906, 0.4559
                    quad 0.4910, 0.4910 to 0.4559, 0.4906
                    line to 0.4403, 0.5047
                    quad 0.4369, 0.5396 to 0.4021, 0.5356
                    line to 0.3851, 0.5479
                    quad 0.3781, 0.5823 to 0.3439, 0.5747
                    line to 0.3257, 0.5852
                    quad 0.3152, 0.6186 to 0.2820, 0.6075
                    line to 0.2628, 0.6160
                    quad 0.2488, 0.6482 to 0.2169, 0.6336
                    line to 0.1969, 0.6401
                    quad 0.1797, 0.6707 to 0.1495, 0.6528
                    line to 0.1289, 0.6572
                    quad 0.1086, 0.6858 to 0.0805, 0.6649
                    line to 0.0595, 0.6671
                    quad 0.0363, 0.6934 to 0.0105, 0.6697
                    line to -0.0105, 0.6697
                    quad -0.0363, 0.6934 to -0.0595, 0.6671
                    line to -0.0805, 0.6649
                    quad -0.1086, 0.6858 to -0.1289, 0.6572
                    line to -0.1495, 0.6528
                    quad -0.1797, 0.6707 to -0.1969, 0.6401
                    line to -0.2169, 0.6336
                    quad -0.2488, 0.6482 to -0.2628, 0.6160
                    line to -0.2820, 0.6075
                    quad -0.3152, 0.6186 to -0.3257, 0.5852
                    line to -0.3439, 0.5747
                    quad -0.3781, 0.5823 to -0.3851, 0.5479
                    line to -0.4021, 0.5356
                    quad -0.4369, 0.5396 to -0.4403, 0.5047
                    line to -0.4559, 0.4906
                    quad -0.4910, 0.4910 to -0.4906, 0.4559
                    line to -0.5047, 0.4403
                    quad -0.5396, 0.4369 to -0.5356, 0.4021
                    line to -0.5479, 0.3851
                    quad -0.5823, 0.3781 to -0.5747, 0.3439
                    line to -0.5852, 0.3257
                    quad -0.6186, 0.3152 to -0.6075, 0.2820
                    line to -0.6160, 0.2628
                    quad -0.6482, 0.2488 to -0.6336, 0.2169
                    line to -0.6401, 0.1969
                    quad -0.6707, 0.1797 to -0.6528, 0.1495
                    line to -0.6572, 0.1289
                    quad -0.6858, 0.1086 to -0.6649, 0.0805
                    line to -0.6671, 0.0595
                    quad -0.6934, 0.0363 to -0.6697, 0.0105
                    line to -0.6697, -0.0105
                    quad -0.6934, -0.0363 to -0.6671, -0.0595
                    line to -0.6649, -0.0805
                    quad -0.6858, -0.1086 to -0.6572, -0.1289
